window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"workspace-connections\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">工作区连接</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>工作区连接允许符合条件的 Team Task 或 @ChatGPT 界面使用公司管理的应用账户，无需每位参与者分别连接个人账户。</p> <p>背景介绍请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\">插件权限和数据共享的工作方式</a>。</p> <p>工作区管理员负责授权受支持的应用账户、管理已保存的连接，并控制哪些人可以发现和使用这些连接。各账户的数据和操作权限由相应服务提供商控制。</p> <p>账户授权请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">连接和管理应用账户（需联网）</a>；周期性任务请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中创建和管理团队任务（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-it-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">工作原理</h2> <p>对于需要使用公司管理账户的 <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">@ChatGPT</a> 或 <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">Team Tasks</a>，可以使用工作区连接。管理员批准访问权限，团队所有者在权限允许时选择可用连接。符合条件的团队和工作流可以重复使用这些连接。</p> <p><strong>连接</strong>用于对应用进行身份验证，使其能够访问某个账户。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-a-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">设置连接</h2> <p><a id=\"before-you-begin\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">开始之前</h3> <p>确认工作区中提供所需应用和身份验证方式，再分配以下职责：</p> <p><strong>工作区管理员：</strong>需要拥有<a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-1-enable-plugin-availability\">管理插件的权限</a>（工作区所有者或管理员），负责创建并授权连接，以及配置谁可以发现、使用和管理它。</p> <p><strong>服务提供商管理员：</strong>负责准备账户并批准对来源服务的访问。对于 Notion 和 Linear，应联系服务提供商管理员；此人可能与用于连接身份验证的账户所有者不同。</p> <p>不同服务提供商的要求各异：Gmail 可能需要单独的用户账户；Drive 访问权限必须在 Google 中配置；当前版本的 GitHub 使用用户账户登录。</p> <p><strong>连接账户：</strong>使用经过批准的账户或服务身份，并仅授予所需资源的访问权限。请使用受支持的身份验证方式，避免依赖员工个人账户。请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 ChatGPT 中连接和管理应用账户（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><strong>连接所有者：</strong>维护授权、协调权限变更并恢复失效的访问。共享前应检查资源范围、读写权限和撤销方式。</p> <p><strong>团队或工作流所有者：</strong>与管理员确认所需资源和操作，再在任务或 @ChatGPT 界面中选择并测试连接。</p> <p><a id=\"create-a-workspace-connection\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">创建工作区连接</h3> <ol> <li> <p>在 Admin Console 中选择工作区，打开“工作区连接” &gt; “+”，然后选择应用。</p> </li> <li> <p>按照应用说明使用提供的身份验证方式。如果系统提示，请启用实时应用访问。</p> </li> <li> <p>对指定账户进行身份验证，或完成应用安装。核实账户或安装状态以及所请求的权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>为已保存的连接设置能说明访问范围的昵称，例如“项目报告：只读访问”。</p> </li> <li> <p>向获准的用户、团队或服务账户授予访问权限。分别检查使用权限和管理权限，然后交由团队或工作流所有者选择并测试。</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"notion--connect-the-intended-workspace-and-content\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"notion-connect-the-intended-workspace-and-content\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"set-up-each-app\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">设置各个应用</h3> <p>请使用应用提供的连接方式，然后配置访问权限，并在预定工作流中测试。</p> <h3 id=\"google-drive\">Google Drive</h3> <p><span id=\"google-drive--authorize-a-google-account\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-drive-authorize-a-google-account\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"authorize-an-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_7\">授权账户</h4> <p>使用经过批准且能够访问所需文件或共享云端硬盘的 Google 账户。</p> <ol> <li> <p>选择 Google 登录，选中要连接的账户，并在批准前检查所请求的访问权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>确认 Google 账户，然后在 ChatGPT 中为连接命名。如果工作流会创建文件，请测试目标位置以及接收者的访问权限。</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"google-drive--use-a-google-service-account\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-drive-use-a-google-service-account\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"use-a-service-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_8\">使用服务账户</h4> <p>如果支持直接使用服务账户进行身份验证，请准备经过批准的 Google Cloud 服务账户和 JSON 密钥。此方式使用服务账户自身的资源访问权限，不需要全网域委派。</p> <ol> <li> <p>将所需文件、文件夹或共享云端硬盘的访问权限授予服务账户邮箱。分别检查读取和写入权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>在受保护的凭据字段中输入完整 JSON 密钥。不要将密钥放入屏幕截图或支持请求消息。</p> </li> <li> <p>保存连接，并尝试读取已与服务账户共享的文件。</p> </li> </ol> <p><strong>请使用共享云端硬盘创建文件。</strong>服务账户必须拥有该硬盘的写入权限。它不能成为个人“My Drive”中的文件所有者。</p> <p>如果找不到文件，请检查是否已与服务账户邮箱共享，以及 ChatGPT 中是否允许该应用执行相应操作。共享文件夹不会自动授予整个 Google Workspace 网域的访问权限。</p> <p>如果 Drive 提供全网域委派，请按照下文的<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\">委派访问流程</a>操作。</p> <h3 id=\"gmail\">Gmail</h3> <p><a id=\"authorize-a-mailbox\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_9\">授权邮箱</h4> <p>如果提供 OAuth，请授权指定的 Gmail 邮箱。如果工作流需要专用邮箱，请向 IT 部门申请单独的用户账户。</p> <ol> <li> <p>选择 Google 登录，选中该邮箱，并在批准前检查所请求的访问权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>检查已保存的连接，并读取一封获准的测试邮件。如果需要发送邮件，请向获准的收件人进行测试，并核实发件人和送达的邮件。</p> </li> </ol> <p>Google 群组不是邮箱。已连接且订阅某个群组的邮箱可以接收群组邮件，但也可能暴露其他邮件。共享之前，请检查邮箱内容和允许执行的操作。</p> <p><span id=\"google-workspace--domain-wide-delegation\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"set-up-domain-wide-delegation\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_10\">设置全网域委派</h4> <p>委派要求请求者是经过验证的员工，并会使用该员工委派的 Google 权限。开始无人值守的工作前，请确认当前体验能够验证请求者身份。<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-drive-use-a-google-service-account\">直接使用 Drive 服务账户访问</a>的工作方式不同。</p> <p>只有在提供此选项时才使用委派。它需要 Google Workspace 超级管理员批准，以及经过批准的 Google Cloud 服务账户、其数字 OAuth 客户端 ID 和完整 JSON 密钥。</p> <ol> <li> <p>选择应用和操作，确认它们所需的准确作用域，并请 Google Workspace 管理员批准。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 Google Admin 中打开 <strong>安全 &gt; 访问权限和数据控件 &gt; API 控件 &gt; 管理全网域委派</strong>。授权数字客户端 ID 和已批准的作用域，并核实已保存的授权。</p> </li> <li> <p>在 ChatGPT 中私密地输入 JSON 密钥。在实际使用此连接的体验中，使用经过验证的请求者和其有权访问的资源进行测试。</p> </li> </ol> <p>如果请求被拒绝，请检查请求者身份、已批准的作用域和资源访问权限。不要仅为消除错误而扩大作用域。</p> <h3 id=\"github\">GitHub</h3> <p><span id=\"github--select-an-app-installation-and-repositories\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"github-select-an-app-installation-and-repositories\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"authorize-a-user-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_11\">授权用户账户</h4> <p>使用组织批准的 GitHub 用户账户（最好是专为此设置创建的账户），并确保它能够访问所需代码库。</p> <p><strong>当前版本暂不支持通过 GitHub 应用登录。</strong></p> <ol> <li> <p>选择 GitHub 用户账户登录，并验证指定账户。</p> </li> <li> <p>在批准连接前，检查账户和所请求的访问权限。</p> </li> <li> <p>保存连接，并从预定工作流中测试已知代码库资源。所需的写入操作应单独测试。</p> </li> </ol> <p>如果找不到代码库，请检查指定账户的 GitHub 访问权限以及 ChatGPT 中允许该应用执行的操作。</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud 使用个人 GitHub 连接。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8?anchor=2-connect-github\">云端设置</a>。</p> <h3 id=\"notion\">Notion</h3> <p><a id=\"prepare-a-dedicated-notion-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"notion_1\">准备专用 Notion 账户</h4> <p>请 Notion 管理员创建经过批准的专用账户，并仅授予所需资源的访问权限。确认该账户已加入工作区。此连接使用该账户的权限。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_12\">配置工作区连接</h4> <p>在 Admin Console &gt; 工作区连接中添加 Notion 插件。通过 Notion MCP 使用指定账户登录，选择工作区，并为连接命名，以便识别工作区和账户。</p> <p>保存连接，并从预定任务或界面中测试已知 Notion 页面。所需的写入操作应单独测试并核实结果。</p> <h3 id=\"linear\">Linear</h3> <p><a id=\"prepare-a-dedicated-linear-account\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"linear_1\">准备专用 Linear 账户</h4> <p>请 Linear 管理员将指定账户作为访客邀请，并将其访问权限限制在所需团队范围内：</p> <ul> <li> <p>打开“设置” → “管理” → “成员” → “邀请”。</p> </li> <li> <p>输入指定账户的电子邮件地址。</p> </li> <li> <p>在“邀请身份...”下选择“访客”。</p> </li> <li> <p>只选择该账户应当访问的 Linear 团队。</p> </li> <li> <p>发送邀请，再使用指定账户接受邀请。</p> </li> </ul> <p>请参阅 <a href=\"https://linear.app/docs/invite-members\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear 邀请说明（需联网）</a>。</p> <p>如果指定账户已经是成员，请 Linear 管理员更新其角色：</p> <ul> <li> <p>打开“设置” → “管理” → “成员”。</p> </li> <li> <p>找到该账户，然后依次点击 ⋯ → “更改角色...” → “访客”。</p> </li> <li> <p>将成员资格限制在预定团队范围内。访客在这些团队中拥有普通成员的功能。请参阅 <a href=\"https://linear.app/docs/members-roles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear 角色（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> </ul> <p><a id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection_1\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_13\">配置工作区连接</h4> <ol> <li> <p>在 Admin Console → 工作区连接中添加 Linear 插件。</p> </li> <li> <p>使用指定账户登录，选择工作区并检查权限。</p> </li> </ol> <p>此连接使用该账户的 Linear 访问权限。从将要使用此连接的任务或界面中，确认它能够读取预定团队中的问题。所需的写入操作应单独测试。</p> <h3 id=\"slack\">Slack</h3> <p><span id=\"slack--configure-the-chatgpt-in-slack-connection\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"slack-configure-the-chatgpt-in-slack-connection\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"test-an-existing-workspace-connection\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection_2\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_14\">配置工作区连接</h4> <p>确认所需的 Slack 工作区、频道、应用安装和管理员批准均已就绪。请使用该界面提供的 <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=configure-company-access\">ChatGPT in Slack 共享连接</a>。个人 Slack 连接和 <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">Dots 的“添加到 Slack”连接</a>是彼此独立的。</p> <p>在获准的频道中测试发送消息，并核实其工作区和发送者。读取和搜索功能需要分别测试；成功发送消息并不能证明这两项功能正常。</p> <p>团队和工作流所有者</p> <p><a id=\"select-and-test\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_15\">选择并测试</h2> <p><a id=\"configure-access-and-select-the-connection\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">配置访问权限并选择连接</h3> <p><strong>工作区管理员：</strong>配置角色访问权限和可用范围；分别检查使用权限和管理权限。向工作流所有者提供连接昵称、账户、获准资源/操作，以及连接所有者的联系方式。</p> <p><strong>团队或工作流所有者：</strong>在权限允许时选择并保存可用连接，然后在预定工作流中测试。如果找不到该连接，请工作区管理员检查访问权限和可用范围。</p> <p><span id=\"configure-access-and-select-the-credential\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"what-each-setting-controls\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_17\">各项设置的作用</h3> <p>为某个连接启用 Slack 或 Microsoft Teams 中的 @ChatGPT，也会启用该连接的团队和服务账户访问选项。只要该连接仍启用 @ChatGPT，这些选项就不能单独关闭。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>设置或权限</strong></th> <th><strong>检查内容</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>外部账户</td> <td>指定账户或应用安装是否能访问所需资源并执行相应操作？</td> </tr> <tr> <td>角色访问</td> <td>获准的人员或服务账户是否可以使用该连接？管理权限应单独检查。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>可用范围</td> <td>目标用户、团队或服务账户能否找到该连接？请检查已配置的受众范围。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>团队或工作流选择</td> <td>是否已为将要使用它的团队或工作流选择并保存该连接？</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"connections-for-teams-and-workflows\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_18\">团队和工作流的连接</h3> <p><a id=\"review-a-teams-connections\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_19\">检查团队连接</h4> <p>请与连接所有者一起检查每个插件的连接昵称、账户和资源访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-connection-for-a-workflow\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_20\">为工作流选择连接</h4> <p>对于 <strong>@ChatGPT</strong>，请打开该界面的<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=configure-company-access\">插件设置</a>并选择连接。保存后重新打开设置，确认选择仍然生效。</p> <p>对于 <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">Team Task</a>，请确认每个应用所选的连接。团队服务账户负责运行任务；每个应用的身份验证方式决定其外部账户。请确认该身份验证方式支持任务运行类型，尤其是在任务要求验证员工身份时。</p> <p><span id=\"test-access-through-the-intended-experience\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"test-the-connection-in-your-workflow\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_21\">在工作流中测试连接</h3> <ol> <li> <p>从预定工作流中读取已知来源，并核实身份和资源。</p> </li> <li> <p>在获准的目标位置测试写入或发送操作，并打开生成的文件、记录或消息进行检查。</p> </li> <li> <p>验证获准用户可以使用连接，而未获授权用户不能使用。检查接收者是否有权访问生成的文件。</p> </li> </ol> <p>连接使用者</p> <p><a id=\"use-workspace-connections\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_22\">使用工作区连接</h2> <p><a id=\"understand-the-connected-accounts-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_23\">了解已连接账户的权限</h3> <p>操作会使用已连接账户的权限，这些权限可能超出你的个人访问权限。OAuth 使用经过授权的账户；直接使用服务账户时则使用该服务身份的权限。某些方式要求验证请求者身份，请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\">Google Workspace 委派</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"use-an-available-workspace-connection\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_24\">使用可用的工作区连接</h3> <ol> <li>如果界面提供该选项，请选择指定连接。对于受管理的 @ChatGPT 界面或 Team Tasks，请与所有者确认所选连接。</li> </ol> <p>每次使用时都无需重新输入指定账户的凭据。如果系统提示登录，请核实连接和正在授权的账户。</p> <p>工作区连接可能可以读取你本人无法打开的来源。来源链接不会自动授予访问权限。生成的文件可能仅对已连接账户可见，因此共享前请检查接收者的访问权限。</p> <p>连接所有者和使用者</p> <p><a id=\"manage-and-troubleshoot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_25\">管理和故障排除</h2> <p><a id=\"manage-changes-and-remove-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_26\">管理变更并移除访问权限</h3> <p>检查连接的昵称、可用范围和角色。</p> <p>如果授权或服务提供商权限发生变更，请连接所有者恢复访问，然后让工作流所有者重新测试。重命名连接不会改变外部权限。</p> <p>停用连接前，请与所有者确认受影响的工作流。移除后，验证这些用户和工作流已无法继续使用该连接。</p> <p>服务提供商处的授权需要单独撤销；停用 ChatGPT 连接不能代替这一步。</p> <p><span id=\"troubleshoot-by-checking-the-failed-layer\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"find-the-right-person-to-resolve-access\"></span></p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-access\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_27\">排查访问问题</h3> <p>如果找不到连接，请确认工作区，并使用<a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=find-the-right-person-to-resolve-access\">访问问题排查表</a>确定应由谁检查角色访问权限和受众范围。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>问题现象</strong></th> <th><strong>可以联系谁</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>找不到连接</td> <td>工作区管理员可以检查你的角色和连接的受众设置。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>连接可用，但任务没有使用</td> <td>界面或团队所有者可以检查工作流的应用配置了哪个工作区连接。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>来源或操作失败</td> <td>连接所有者可以检查连接使用的身份，以及该身份能否访问相应资源或执行操作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>可以阅读摘要，但无法打开来源</td> <td>来源所有者可以检查你对原始页面或文件的访问权限。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>接收者无法打开生成的文件</td> <td>文件所有者可以检查文件共享设置。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>重试失败的写入或发送操作前，请先检查目标位置。即使出现错误，操作也可能已经完成；再次重试可能造成重复。</p> <p><a id=\"related-guides\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_28\">相关指南</h2> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">ChatGPT Work 云安全</a></p> </li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"workspace-connections\">Workspace connections</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>A workspace connection lets an eligible Team Task or @ChatGPT surface use a company-managed app account without each participant connecting a personal account.</p> <p>For background, see <a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a?anchor=how-permissions-and-data-sharing-work\">how plugin permissions and data sharing work</a>.</p> <p>Workspace admins authorize supported app accounts, manage saved connections, and control who can find and use them. The provider controls each account’s data and action permissions.</p> <p>See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Connecting and managing app accounts (online)</a> for account authorization, and <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001540\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and managing team tasks in ChatGPT (online)</a> for recurring work.</p> <h2 id=\"how-it-works\">How it works</h2> <p>Use connections for <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">@ChatGPT</a> or <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">Team Tasks</a> that need company-managed accounts. Admins approve access; team owners select available connections where permitted. Connections can be reused across eligible teams and workflows.</p> <p>A <strong>connection</strong> authenticates an app to an account.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-a-connection\">Set up a connection</h2> <h3 id=\"before-you-begin\">Before you begin</h3> <p>Confirm the app and authentication method are available in your workspace, then assign these responsibilities:</p> <p><strong>Workspace administrator:</strong> With <a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420?anchor=step-1-enable-plugin-availability\">permission to manage plugins</a> (workspace owner or admin), create and authorize the connection and configure who can find, use, and manage it.</p> <p><strong>Provider administrator:</strong> Provision accounts and approve source-service access. For Notion and Linear, involve the provider administrator; this person may differ from the account authenticating the connection.</p> <p>Provider requirements differ: Gmail may need a separate user account, Drive access must be configured in Google, and GitHub uses user-account sign-in at launch.</p> <p><strong>Connection account:</strong> Use an approved account or service identity with only the required resource access. Follow the supported authentication method and avoid reliance on an employee’s personal account. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001494-connecting-and-managing-app-accounts-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Connecting and managing app accounts in ChatGPT (online)</a>.</p> <p><strong>Connection owner:</strong> Maintain authorization, coordinate permission changes, and restore failed access. Review resource scope, read/write permissions, and revocation before sharing.</p> <p><strong>Team or workflow owner:</strong> Agree on required resources and actions with the admin, then select and test the connection in the task or @ChatGPT surface.</p> <h3 id=\"create-a-workspace-connection\">Create a workspace connection</h3> <ol> <li> <p>In the Admin Console, select the workspace and open Workspace connections &gt; +. Choose the app.</p> </li> <li> <p>Follow the app’s instructions for the offered authentication method. Enable real-time app access if prompted.</p> </li> <li> <p>Authenticate the designated account or complete app installation. Verify the account or installation and requested permissions.</p> </li> <li> <p>Give the saved connection a nickname that describes its access, such as “Project reporting: read access.”</p> </li> <li> <p>Grant access to approved users, teams, or service accounts. Review use and management permissions separately, then hand off to the team or workflow owner for selection and testing.</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"notion--connect-the-intended-workspace-and-content\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"notion-connect-the-intended-workspace-and-content\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"set-up-each-app\">Set up each app</h3> <p>Use the method offered for your app, then configure access and test it in the intended workflow.</p> <h3 id=\"google-drive\">Google Drive</h3> <p><span id=\"google-drive--authorize-a-google-account\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-drive-authorize-a-google-account\"></span></p> <h4 id=\"authorize-an-account\">Authorize an account</h4> <p>Use an approved Google account with access to the required files or shared drives.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Choose Google sign-in, select the account you want to connect, and review the requested access before approving.</p> </li> <li> <p>Confirm the Google account, then name the connection in ChatGPT. If the workflow creates files, test the destination and recipients’ access.</p> </li> </ol> <p><span id=\"google-drive--use-a-google-service-account\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-drive-use-a-google-service-account\"></span></p> <h4 id=\"use-a-service-account\">Use a service account</h4> <p>If direct service-account authentication is offered, prepare an approved Google Cloud service account and JSON key. This uses the service account’s resource access, without domain-wide delegation.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Give the service-account email access to the required files, folders, or shared drives. Check read and write permissions separately.</p> </li> <li> <p>Enter the complete JSON key in the protected credential field. Keep it out of screenshots and support messages.</p> </li> <li> <p>Save the connection and try reading a file shared with the service account.</p> </li> </ol> <p><strong>Use a shared drive to create files.</strong> The service account needs write permission there. It cannot own files in a personal My Drive.</p> <p>For missing files, check sharing with the service-account email and the app’s allowed actions in ChatGPT. Folder sharing does not grant access across the Google Workspace domain.</p> <p>If Drive offers domain-wide delegation, follow the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\">delegated-access procedure below</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"gmail\">Gmail</h3> <h4 id=\"authorize-a-mailbox\">Authorize a mailbox</h4> <p>If OAuth is offered, authorize the designated Gmail mailbox. Ask IT for a separate user account if the workflow needs its own mailbox.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Choose Google sign-in, select the mailbox, and review the requested access before approving.</p> </li> <li> <p>Check the saved connection and read an approved test message. If sending is required, test an approved recipient and verify the sender and delivered message.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Google Groups are not mailboxes. A connected mailbox subscribed to a group can receive its messages but may also expose other mail. Review its contents and allowed actions before sharing.</p> <p><span id=\"google-workspace--domain-wide-delegation\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\"></span></p> <h4 id=\"set-up-domain-wide-delegation\">Set up domain-wide delegation</h4> <p>Delegation requires a verified requesting employee and uses their delegated Google permissions. Before unattended work, confirm the experience can establish that requester. <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-drive-use-a-google-service-account\">Direct Drive service-account access</a> works differently.</p> <p>Use delegation only where offered. It requires Google Workspace super-admin approval and an approved Google Cloud service account with its numeric OAuth client ID and complete JSON key.</p> <ol> <li> <p>Select the apps and actions, obtain their exact required scopes, and have your Google Workspace administrator approve them.</p> </li> <li> <p>In Google Admin, open <strong>Security &gt; Access and data control &gt; API controls &gt; Manage Domain Wide Delegation</strong>. Authorize the numeric client ID and approved scopes; verify the saved grant.</p> </li> <li> <p>Enter the JSON key privately in ChatGPT. Test in the experience that will use the connection, with a verified requester and a resource they can access.</p> </li> </ol> <p>For denied requests, check the requester, approved scopes, and resource access. Do not broaden scopes just to clear an error.</p> <h3 id=\"github\">GitHub</h3> <p><span id=\"github--select-an-app-installation-and-repositories\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"github-select-an-app-installation-and-repositories\"></span></p> <h4 id=\"authorize-a-user-account\">Authorize a user account</h4> <p>Use an organization-approved GitHub user account, preferably dedicated to this setup, with access to the required repositories.</p> <p><strong>GitHub app sign-in is unavailable for this launch.</strong></p> <ol> <li> <p>Choose GitHub user-account sign-in and authenticate the designated account.</p> </li> <li> <p>Review the account and requested access before approving the connection.</p> </li> <li> <p>Save and test a known repository resource from the intended workflow. Test required write actions separately.</p> </li> </ol> <p>If a repository is missing, check the designated account’s GitHub access and the app’s allowed actions in ChatGPT.</p> <p>Codex Security Cloud uses a personal GitHub connection. See <a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8?anchor=2-connect-github\">Cloud setup</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"notion\">Notion</h3> <h4 id=\"prepare-a-dedicated-notion-account\">Prepare a dedicated Notion account</h4> <p>Ask your Notion administrator to provision an approved dedicated account and grant only the required resource access. Confirm workspace membership. The connection uses this account’s permissions.</p> <h4 id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection\">Configure the workspace connection</h4> <p>In Admin Console &gt; Workspace connections, add the Notion plugin. Sign in as the designated account through Notion MCP, select the workspace, and name the connection to identify the workspace and account.</p> <p>Save and test a known Notion page from the intended task or surface. Test required writes separately and verify the result.</p> <h3 id=\"linear\">Linear</h3> <h4 id=\"prepare-a-dedicated-linear-account\">Prepare a dedicated Linear account</h4> <p>Ask a Linear administrator to invite the designated account as a guest and limit its access to the teams it needs:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Open Settings → Administration → Members → Invite.</p> </li> <li> <p>Enter the designated account’s email address.</p> </li> <li> <p>Under Invite as…, choose Guest.</p> </li> <li> <p>Select only the Linear teams the account should access.</p> </li> <li> <p>Send the invitation and accept it as the designated account.</p> </li> </ul> <p>See <a href=\"https://linear.app/docs/invite-members\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear invitation instructions (online)</a>.</p> <p>If the designated account is already a Member, ask a Linear administrator to update its role:</p> <ul> <li> <p>Open Settings → Administration → Members.</p> </li> <li> <p>Find the account and click ⋯ → Change role… → Guest.</p> </li> <li> <p>Limit membership to intended teams. Guests have normal member capabilities within those teams. See <a href=\"https://linear.app/docs/members-roles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Linear roles (online)</a>.</p> </li> </ul> <h4 id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection_1\">Configure the workspace connection</h4> <ol> <li> <p>In Admin Console → Workspace connections, add the Linear plugin.</p> </li> <li> <p>Sign in as the designated account, select the workspace, and review permissions.</p> </li> </ol> <p>The connection uses that account’s Linear access. From the task or surface that will use it, confirm that the connection can read an issue in an intended team. Test any required write actions separately.</p> <h3 id=\"slack\">Slack</h3> <p><span id=\"slack--configure-the-chatgpt-in-slack-connection\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"slack-configure-the-chatgpt-in-slack-connection\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"test-an-existing-workspace-connection\"></span></p> <h4 id=\"configure-the-workspace-connection_2\">Configure the workspace connection</h4> <p>Confirm the required Slack workspace, channels, app installation, and admin approval. Use the surface’s <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=configure-company-access\">shared ChatGPT in Slack connection</a>. Personal Slack connections and the <a href=\"#/article/a-4b4aabd54f9e5c9c?anchor=slack\">dots Add to Slack connection</a> are separate.</p> <p>Test a post in an approved channel and verify its workspace and sender. Test reading and search separately; a successful post does not verify either.</p> <p>Team and workflow owners</p> <h2 id=\"select-and-test\">Select and test</h2> <h3 id=\"configure-access-and-select-the-connection\">Configure access and select the connection</h3> <p><strong>Workspace administrator:</strong> Configure role access and availability; review use and management permissions separately. Give the workflow owner the connection nickname, account, approved resources/actions, and owner’s contact details.</p> <p><strong>Team or workflow owner:</strong> Select and save the available connection where permitted, then test it in the intended workflow. If missing, have the workspace admin check access and availability.</p> <p><span id=\"configure-access-and-select-the-credential\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"what-each-setting-controls\">What each setting controls</h3> <p>Enabling @ChatGPT in Slack or Microsoft Teams for a connection also enables that connection’s team and service-account access options. These cannot be disabled independently while @ChatGPT is enabled for that connection.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>Setting or permission</strong></th> <th><strong>What to check</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>External account</td> <td>Can the designated account or installation access the required resources and actions?</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Role access</td> <td>Can the approved person or service account use the connection? Check management permissions separately.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Availability</td> <td>Can the intended users, teams, or service accounts find the connection? Check the configured audience.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Team or workflow selection</td> <td>Is the connection selected and saved for the team or workflow that will use it?</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h3 id=\"connections-for-teams-and-workflows\">Connections for teams and workflows</h3> <h4 id=\"review-a-teams-connections\">Review a team's connections</h4> <p>Check each plugin’s connection nickname, account, and resource access with the connection owner.</p> <h4 id=\"choose-a-connection-for-a-workflow\">Choose a connection for a workflow</h4> <p>For <strong>@ChatGPT</strong>, open the <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=configure-company-access\">surface's plugin settings</a> and select the connection. Save, then reopen settings to check the selection.</p> <p>For a <a href=\"#/article/a-81de09346a07fee6?anchor=create-a-team-task\">Team Task</a>, confirm the selected connection for each app. The team service account runs the task; each app’s authentication method determines its external account. Confirm that method supports the task’s run type, especially if it requires a verified employee.</p> <p><span id=\"test-access-through-the-intended-experience\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"test-the-connection-in-your-workflow\">Test the connection in your workflow</h3> <ol> <li> <p>Read a known source from the intended workflow. Verify the identity and resource.</p> </li> <li> <p>Test writes or sends at an approved destination and open the resulting file, record, or message.</p> </li> <li> <p>Verify that an approved user can use the connection and an unauthorized user cannot. Check recipients’ access to generated files.</p> </li> </ol> <p>Connection users</p> <h2 id=\"use-workspace-connections\">Use workspace connections</h2> <h3 id=\"understand-the-connected-accounts-permissions\">Understand the connected account's permissions</h3> <p>Actions use the connected account’s permissions, which may exceed your personal access. OAuth uses the authorized account; direct service-account access uses that identity. Some methods require a verified requester; see <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=google-workspace-domain-wide-delegation\">Google Workspace delegation</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"use-an-available-workspace-connection\">Use an available workspace connection</h3> <ol> <li>If offered, choose the designated connection. For managed @ChatGPT surfaces or Team Tasks, confirm the selection with the owner.</li> </ol> <p>You do not re-enter the designated account’s credentials for each use. If prompted to sign in, verify the connection and account being authorized.</p> <p>A workspace connection may read sources you cannot open. Source links do not grant access. Generated files may be private to the connected account, so check recipients’ access before sharing.</p> <p>Connection owners and users</p> <h2 id=\"manage-and-troubleshoot\">Manage and troubleshoot</h2> <h3 id=\"manage-changes-and-remove-access\">Manage changes and remove access</h3> <p>Review the connection’s nickname, availability, and roles.</p> <p>If authorization or provider permissions change, have the connection owner restore access and the workflow owner retest. Renaming a connection does not change external permissions.</p> <p>Before disabling a connection, identify affected workflows with their owners. After removal, verify those users and workflows can no longer use it.</p> <p>Revoke provider authorization separately; disabling the ChatGPT connection does not replace this step.</p> <p><span id=\"troubleshoot-by-checking-the-failed-layer\"></span></p> <p><span id=\"find-the-right-person-to-resolve-access\"></span></p> <h3 id=\"troubleshoot-access\">Troubleshoot access</h3> <p>For a missing connection, verify the workspace and use the <a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=find-the-right-person-to-resolve-access\">access troubleshooting table</a> to find who can check role access and audience.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th><strong>What happens</strong></th> <th><strong>Who can help</strong></th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>The connection is missing</td> <td>Your workspace administrator can check your role and the connection’s audience settings.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>It is available but the job does not use it</td> <td>The surface or Team owner can check which workspace connection is configured for the workflow’s app.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A source or action fails</td> <td>The connection owner can check which identity the connection uses and whether it can access the resource or action.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>You can read a summary but not its source</td> <td>The source owner can check your access to the original page or file.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>A recipient cannot open a generated file</td> <td>The file owner can review its sharing settings.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Before retrying a failed write or send, check the destination. The action may have completed despite the error; retrying could create duplicates.</p> <h2 id=\"related-guides\">Related guides</h2> <ul> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a></p> </li> <li> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">ChatGPT Work cloud security</a></p> </li> </ul>"};
